# Bandit Level 11 → Level 12

## Goal
he password for the next level is stored in the file data.txt, where all lowercase (a-z) and uppercase (A-Z) letters have been rotated by 13 positions

## Commands used
- cat data.txt | tr 'a-zA-Z' 'n-za-mN-ZA-M'

## Explanation
- 'cat data.txt' read file data.txt
- 'tr '[original characters] [replacement characters]'' tr means replace characters with other characters
- 'a-z' all lowercase letter,a through z
- 'A-Z' all uppercase letters,A through Z
- 'n-za-m' n through z, followed by a through m in lower case
- 'N-ZA-M' N through Z followed by A through M in upper case

## Result
Was able to receive the password for the next level.

## What I learned
How to change the position of letters in linux.
